{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":494087,"name":"Wes Anderson","username":"Wes_Anderson","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/w/0ea827/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T13:38:44.217Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494087-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494087-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494087-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494087-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile testing a custom teammate (“Scout”) that watched a background process and reported updates in chat, two problems showed up:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe teammate stopped answering chat (looked hung) while parked on long AwaitShell-style waits.\u003cbr\u003e\nAfter deleting and recreating that teammate, the UI accepted typed messages but showed Failed to send, and the agent transcript stayed empty. Another existing teammate (e.g. Annie) still worked. Quitting/reopening the app and recreating the agent again fixed delivery.\u003cbr\u003e\nEnvironment\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot desktop 0.55.0\u003cbr\u003e\nWindows 11 Home Version 10.0.26200 Build 26200\u003cbr\u003e\nMultiple teammates on one shared Grok Bot computer\u003cbr\u003e\nNew teammate created via another bot / CreateAgent flow\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494087-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494087-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA — Hung / no replies while “working”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCreate a teammate whose job is to watch a long-running shell/background stream and post short updates to chat.\u003cbr\u003e\nHave it wait for the next event with a long await (on the order of minutes, e.g. ~180s), then post, then wait again in the same turn chain.\u003cbr\u003e\nWhile it is waiting, send normal chat messages (“hi”, “stop”).\u003cbr\u003e\nObserve: delayed or missing replies; agent appears stuck until the wait ends or processes are killed externally.\u003cbr\u003e\nB — Failed to send after delete + recreate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDelete the hung teammate from the sidebar (right-click → Delete).\u003cbr\u003e\nRecreate a teammate with the same name via another agent.\u003cbr\u003e\nOpen the new teammate chat and send messages.\u003cbr\u003e\nObserve: bubbles appear with Failed to send (Resend / Delete).\u003cbr\u003e\nConfirm: agent-side transcript has no entries (messages never arrived).\u003cbr\u003e\nConfirm: other teammates still send/receive normally.\u003cbr\u003e\nFully quit and reopen Grok Bot; delete the broken teammate; create again.\u003cbr\u003e\nObserve: messaging works again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494087-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494087-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUser chat should interrupt or queue ahead of long background waits so the teammate stays responsive.\u003cbr\u003e\nA newly created teammate should accept messages immediately (no Failed to send).\u003cbr\u003e\nIf create is incomplete, the UI should not pretend the message was composed successfully without delivery.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494087-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494087-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494087-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494087-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot desktop 0.55.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494087-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494087-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494087-additional-information-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494087-additional-information-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eActual Behavior\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLong wait loops made the teammate look dead in chat.\u003cbr\u003e\nPost-recreate instance: UI showed Failed to send; no agent transcript; other bots fine.\u003cbr\u003e\nWorkaround: app restart + delete/recreate restored messaging (~2–3s replies in our follow-up test).\u003cbr\u003e\nRoot cause (our read — for engineering)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHang: Agent turn stayed blocked on long shell awaits chained with chat posts. Platform may not surface/prioritize new user messages until that tool call finishes, so the chat looks broken even though the agent “exists.”\u003cbr\u003e\nFailed to send: Recreation produced a sidebar agent whose message pipeline was not fully wired (client send failed; empty transcript). Points to a race/incomplete provision after CreateAgent + delete, not user error. App restart + fresh create cleared it.\u003cbr\u003e\nWorkaround / fix that worked for us\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStop leftover background listener processes on the shared computer.\u003cbr\u003e\nPrefer delete + recreate over “Update Grok Bot’s Computer” for a single hung agent (Update affects all bots’ machine, reinstalls tools, can jostle secrets).\u003cbr\u003e\nIf recreate shows Failed to send: fully quit Grok Bot → reopen → delete that agent → create again.\u003cbr\u003e\nFor watchers: keep awaits short (seconds, not minutes), end turns cleanly, and always answer user/stop before restarting a watch.\u003cbr\u003e\nAsk\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCan new user messages preempt or cancel long AwaitShell waits?\u003cbr\u003e\nCan CreateAgent / post-delete create guarantee the chat send path is ready before the teammate appears in the sidebar?\u003cbr\u003e\nBetter client error when send fails (and avoid showing a “sent-looking” bubble that only fails after)?\u003cbr\u003e\nHappy to provide timestamps or more logs if useful.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494087-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494087-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T21:13:40.605Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":12,"reads":6,"readers_count":5,"score":61.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":172032,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-teammate-unresponsive-after-long-tool-waits-recreated-agent-shows-failed-to-send-until-app-restart-recreate","display_username":"Wes Anderson","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136160,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-teammate-unresponsive-after-long-tool-waits-recreated-agent-shows-failed-to-send-until-app-restart-recreate/172032/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":494375,"name":"Kevin Neilson","username":"kevinn","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/kevinn/{size}/101206_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T21:15:16.276Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/wes_anderson\"\u003e@Wes_Anderson\u003c/a\u003e Thanks for the post. What you saw isn’t how this is supposed to work, and it wasn’t caused by anything in your setup. It lines up with the Grok Bot service degradation on \u003ca href=\"http://status.cursor.com\"\u003estatus.cursor.com\u003c/a\u003e earlier today, which is resolved now. Scout was not stuck on the shell wait, and the recreated bot was not mis-wired. Your messages reached us and were accepted, but the turn behind them never ran, so the app stopped waiting and showed “Failed to send”. The third Scout started answering because the service had recovered by then, not because of the restart.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn your questions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA new message from you is meant to interrupt whatever the bot is doing, including a long wait on a shell command, and start on your message right away. That happened three times in that same Scout chat this morning. Each “hi” or “stop” cancelled the running step within about a second. The one that did not was when this service issue kicked in.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA newly created bot should be ready to chat immediately. The recreated Scout hit the same stall on its very first turn, which is why it never answered.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“Failed to send” was misleading here, since the message did reach us. We’ve let the team know.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf something like this happens again, check \u003ca href=\"http://status.cursor.com\"\u003estatus.cursor.com\u003c/a\u003e first, and hold off on deleting and recreating the bot. The history stays with the original, and a new bot can hit the same stall. If a bot is still silent well after the status page is clear, reply here with the bot name and the time of your last message and I’ll take a look.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T21:15:16.276Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":26.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":172032,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-teammate-unresponsive-after-long-tool-waits-recreated-agent-shows-failed-to-send-until-app-restart-recreate","display_username":"Kevin Neilson","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://status.cursor.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Cursor Status","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":105146,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-teammate-unresponsive-after-long-tool-waits-recreated-agent-shows-failed-to-send-until-app-restart-recreate/172032/7","reactions":[{"id":"+1","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":494394,"name":"Wes Anderson","username":"Wes_Anderson","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/w/0ea827/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T21:56:18.526Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eKevin,  Thanks for the quick reply.  My bots have this locked in should it happen again.  Watching the Grok Bot workshop and learning a lot.  Thanks Wes\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T21:56:18.705Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":45.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":172032,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-teammate-unresponsive-after-long-tool-waits-recreated-agent-shows-failed-to-send-until-app-restart-recreate","display_username":"Wes Anderson","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136160,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":"Automatically removed quote of whole previous post.","can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-teammate-unresponsive-after-long-tool-waits-recreated-agent-shows-failed-to-send-until-app-restart-recreate/172032/8","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":494396,"name":"Landon Taylor","username":"Landon_Taylor","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/ed655f/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T22:14:12.698Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote group-CursorStaff\" data-username=\"kevinn\" data-display-name=\"Kevin Neilson\" data-post=\"7\" data-topic=\"17203